.TH PUTTYMOD 1 "August 2026" "puttymod" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
puttymod \- PuTTyMOD, a patched and rebranded PuTTY SSH/Telnet client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B puttymod
.RI [ options ] " " [ user@ ] host
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B puttymod
is a personal fork of
.BR putty (1),
the free SSH and Telnet client, carrying a set of local usability
patches on top of unmodified upstream PuTTY networking/crypto code:
.IP \(bu 2
a runtime interface translated into 25 languages, chosen from the
Design/Language settings panel;
.IP \(bu 2
a green/red online\-offline indicator on every saved session, checked
asynchronously against that session's own host and port;
.IP \(bu 2
one\-click colour theme presets (Design/Themes), applied to both the
settings dialog chrome and the terminal's own colour scheme;
.IP \(bu 2
password\-protected export/import of saved sessions as
.B .pex
files;
.IP \(bu 2
an optional encrypted auto\-login password, stored at rest under
.IR $HOME/.putty/.pwkey .
.PP
Command\-line options, saved\-session file format, and the underlying
SSH/Telnet/serial protocol support are unchanged from upstream PuTTY;
see
.BR putty (1)
(package
.BR putty ,
if installed) for the full reference, or the Help menu inside the
application itself.
.SH FILES
.I $HOME/.putty/sessions/
.RS
Saved session profiles (same format as upstream PuTTY).
.RE
.I $HOME/.putty/global\-appearance
.RS
This fork's local\-patch settings: interface language, colour theme,
dialog font/opacity. Seeded on first run with the Tokyo Night theme
and English.
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR putty (1),
.BR plink (1),
.BR puttygen (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Upstream PuTTY is written and maintained by Simon Tatham and
contributors; see
.I /usr/share/doc/puttymod/copyright
for the full list. This fork's local patches are maintained
separately from upstream.
